 "author": "Rally Raid samples",
 "description": "Patterned after the Dakar's \"dune marathon\" days (the Atlantic-side dune sea is the Namib equivalent of the Erg stages): a short road transfer north out of Terrace Bay, then 60+ km of pure off-piste through the coastal dune belt to the Mowe Bay ranger station. Realistic: long straight CAP legs, few waypoints, a WPC to stop competitors running the beach instead of the dunes, a WPS on the big slip face, and an eclipse WPE that only opens after the WPS is taken.",
